The Rust Programming Language (rust-lang/rust)
  https://github.com/rust-lang/rust
  Copyright the Rust project contributors.
  - crates/tide-std/src/io/shared.rs: much of the file is adapted, with
    changes, from Rust's io implementation (library/core/src/io,
    library/alloc/src/io, library/std/src/io): the Read, Write, BufRead and
    Seek provided methods, the Bytes, Chain, Take, Split and Lines
    adapters, BufReader,
    BufWriter and its buffer guard, the formatting adapter behind write_fmt,
    and ErrorKind's message table.
  - crates/tide-std/src/convert.rs: the integer truncation pairs mirror
    core's integer_widen_truncate list.
  - tide-std mirrors the public API of Rust's standard library (item names,
    signatures, and Display messages) in the modules it reimplements or
    wraps, such as collections and sync::mpsc.
  - conformance/cases/memory/closure_fnptr_rustc_known_bug.rs: changed by Tide
    from tests/ui/implied-bounds/implied-bounds-on-nested-references-plus-variance-2.rs
    at commit 5f4effd579500175af844241eb179e756190f1e7.
  - These red-team cases in conformance/cases/memory/ follow the public
    reproductions in rust-lang/rust issues: escape_fn_trait_routes.rs
    (#25860), escape_dyn_overlap_transmute.rs (#57893),
    escape_hrtb_supertrait.rs (#84591), and
    escape_projection_implied_bounds.rs (#100051).

